You may want to adopt it to better suit your taste.

My udev installs it up automatically for me with this simple rule:
-------------------------
ACTION=3D=3D"add", KERNEL=3D=3D"event[0-9]*", \=20
	ATTRS{phys}=3D=3D"GPIO/serio[0-9]*/input[0-9]*", \=20
	RUN+=3D"/usr/bin/input-kbd -f /etc/mailboard.map %n"
-------------------------

If you are using Angstrom (or other OpenEmbedded generated distribution=
), you=20
may want to give my simple recipes/input-utils/input-utils.bb recipe a =
try:
-------------------------
PV =3D "20081014-${SRCREV}"
SRCREV =3D "101501"
SRC_URI =3D "http://dl.bytesex.org/cvs-snapshots/input-${PV}.tar.gz \
	file://fix-makefiles.patch;patch=3D1"
LICENSE =3D "GPL"
inherit autotools
S =3D "${WORKDIR}/input"
PACKAGES_prepend =3D "input-kbd input-remote "
=46ILES_input-kbd =3D "/usr/bin/input-kbd"
=46ILES_input-remote =3D "/usr/bin/input-send /usr/bin/input-recv"
--------------------------

and recipes/input-utils/files/fix-makefiles.patch:
--------------------------
--- input/mk/Variables.mk.orig	2008-10-14 12:27:01.000000000 +0200
+++ input/mk/Variables.mk	2010-03-29 17:11:58.000000000 +0200
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ MOC             ?=3D $(if $(QTDIR),$(QTDIR
=20
 STRIP		?=3D -s
 INSTALL		?=3D install
-INSTALL_BINARY  :=3D $(INSTALL) $(STRIP)
+INSTALL_BINARY  :=3D $(INSTALL)
 INSTALL_SCRIPT  :=3D $(INSTALL)
 INSTALL_DATA	:=3D $(INSTALL) -m 644
 INSTALL_DIR	:=3D $(INSTALL) -d
--------------------------

After putting the above two files in your local OE overlay, building th=
e=20
package(s) with "bitbake input-utils" and refreshing your repository Pa=
ckeges=20
list, all you need is running "opkg install input-kbd" on your Delta.

Have fun,
